@api = http://localhost:5100
@worker = http://localhost:5200

### 1. Register a user: 201 with the user id. The saga starts and the worker "sends" the verification code.
POST {{api}}/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@example.com" }

### 2. Invalid email: 400 with the validation errors (FluentValidation through the MediatR pipeline).
POST {{api}}/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana" }

### 3. Read the code the worker would have emailed.
GET {{worker}}/emails

### 4. Status while the saga waits: userStatus PendingConfirmation, sagaState AwaitingConfirmation.
# Replace the id with the one returned in step 1.
GET {{api}}/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 5. Wrong code: 200 (accepted for the saga), the saga ignores it and keeps waiting.
POST {{api}}/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "000000" }

### 6. Malformed code: 400 before anything is published.
POST {{api}}/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "12ab" }

### 7. Right code: 200. The saga activates the user, orders the welcome email and finishes.
POST {{api}}/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "123456" }

### 8. Status after confirming: userStatus Active, sagaState null. Confirming again returns 409.
GET {{api}}/registrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 9. Unknown user: 404.
GET {{api}}/registrations/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
